<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malik Kafur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1316">1316</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malik Kafur was a general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a>, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, in the early fourteenth century. He led the sultanate's most spectacular campaigns into southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, extracting tribute from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> kingdom and sacking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> treasury at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>. By 1311 nearly every major southern Indian power had submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His general <b>Malik Kafur</b> led the most spectacular campaigns in the sultanate's history.</blockquote><a href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The last major war was against the Delhi Sultanate: <b>Malik Kafur</b> captured Dwarasamudra in 1311, and Veera Ballala III fought on against Delhi’s governors and the Madurai Sultanate.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hoysala-empire">Hoysala Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Pandyas were less able to resist the armies of the Delhi Sultanate, whose mobile cavalry under <b>Malik Kafur</b> raided Madurai in 1311 while the kingdom was divided by civil war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/later-pandyan-empire">Later Pandyan Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…service could carry them far: after Firuz Shah’s death his old slaves turned against Sultan Abu Bakr Shah and had Nasir ud-Din Muhammad Shah placed on the throne, and under the Khaljis the slave general <b>Malik Kafur</b>, born to a Hindu family, had held power himself in 1316.</blockquote><a href="/societies/delhi-sultanate">Social Hierarchy of the Delhi Sultanate</a></li><li><blockquote>After <b>Malik Kafur's</b> campaigns, the Delhi Sultanate governed the Madurai region, known as Ma'bar, through officials.</blockquote><a href="/state/madurai-sultanate">Madurai Sultanate</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khambhat">Khambhat</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=22.31,72.62&amp;year=1306" aria-label="Khambhat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6495 1340 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Malik Kafur"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6945 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6945 1610h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=22.31,72.62&amp;year=1306">What was here in 1306? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
